# parse
- label: Source auto-detection checks filepath for magic substrings: opencode:// prefix, .codex/, .cursor/, .factory/, .grok/; defaults to claude
  command: grep -qE "opencode://|\.codex/|\.factory/|\.grok/" src/parse/index.js
- label: parseSession routes all six supported sources through parsers that return the unified Session shape: sessionId, source, cwd, model, gitBranch, startTime, endTime, durationMs, eventCount, events, stats, plus public path and sessionHash
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'parseSession returns unified shape for all supported sources' test/parse.test.js
  tags: [parse-session-shape, implemented]
- label: user and assistant Event text is truncated to 500 chars; tool_result text to 1000 chars
  command: grep -q "500" src/parse/parse-claude.js
- label: normalizeToolName() maps 20+ variant names to canonical forms (bash/shell/execute → Bash, read/read_file → Read, etc.)
  command: grep -qE "normalizeToolName|Bash|Read|Edit|Write" src/parse/parse-enrich.js
- label: error detection uses regex pattern matching on tool_result text: Error:, exit code [1-9], ENOENT, EACCES, SyntaxError, etc.
  command: grep -qE "Error:|exit code|ENOENT|EACCES" src/parse/parse-enrich.js
- label: parseSession skips malformed non-empty JSONL lines after parseJsonlLine logs the parse error; when a JSONL session omits sessionId, cwd, model, and gitBranch, the returned Session keeps those fields null
  id: oil
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'parseSession skips malformed JSONL lines and returns null defaults for missing metadata' test/parse.test.js
  tags: [parse-malformed-defaults, implemented]
- label: Factory, Grok, and OpenCode parser token handling is source-aware rather than zero-filled: Factory assistant turns get buildSession-estimated output tokens when no explicit usage exists, Grok signals.json contextTokensUsed is distributed as assistant input tokens, and OpenCode step-finish parts roll up input/output/cache tokens
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'assistant text and multiple tool_use blocks with enrichment|signals.json contextTokensUsed distributes input tokens across assistant turns|step-finish tokens rollup including cache read/write|estimates output tokens from text and toolCalls when all outputs are zero|estimates input tokens from matching tool_result text' test/parse/parse-factory.test.js test/parse/parse-grok.test.js test/parse/parse-opencode.test.js test/parse/parse-session-build.test.js
  tags: [parse-token-facts, implemented]
- label: summarizeInput() extracts the relevant parameter per tool type for display (Bash→command, Read/Write/Edit→filepath, WebSearch→query, etc.)
  command: grep -q "summarizeInput" src/parse/parse-enrich.js
- parseSession (and buildSession used by all six parsers) never throws RangeError or crashes on events containing missing, null, invalid, non-ISO, or non-date-parseable timestamp values from source jsonl/sqlite data; such bad timestamps are excluded from startTime/endTime/duration calculation (falling back to other good timestamps if present, or null startTime/endTime when no event carries a valid timestamp), while other event data is still processed; parse always succeeds and returns a valid Session object for partially malformed time data @implemented
- Grok parser (parseGrok) includes all user messages extracted from chat_history.jsonl (after extractUserQuery), truncating long ones (>500 chars) with capContent exactly like the claude, codex, cursor, factory, and opencode parsers; it does not silently drop user events whose raw text length >=5000 (the previous length guard is removed for consistency and no data loss on realistic long prompts) @implemented
- parseOpenCode safely recovers from malformed or unparseable JSON in SQLite message.data and part.data columns by skipping the bad row/part (try/catch around each JSON.parse, like jsonl line handling in other parsers); additionally, the node:sqlite require/create DatabaseSync does not emit ExperimentalWarning during parse (suppressed at load point for this code path) @implemented
- safeSlice is defined exactly once server-side in parse.js and imported by server.js; no duplicate server-side safeSlice definition exists in the src/ directory @implemented
- All shared helper functions and constants (errorPattern, normalizeToolName, summarizeInput, extractToolResultText, isMcpTool, parseMcpName, extractMcpInfo, isWebTool, extractWebInfo, isAgentTool, extractAgentInfo, buildSession, estimateMissingTokens, computeStats) are defined in parse.js before the first parser function (parseClaude), eliminating any hoisting dependency on function/const declarations below their first use site @implemented
- normalizeToolName uses a module-scope lookup map instead of recreating a const map object on every call, eliminating repeated object allocation during batch parsing @implemented
- buildIndex updates _indexFileMtime, _indexFileCache, _resultMapCache, and _resultMapKey in-memory after writeFileSync so the next call with identical sessions returns the cached Map instantly without re-reading the disk index file @spec @implemented
- indexCodex uses indexOf-based line iteration instead of split(newline) which creates a large intermediate array, matching indexClaude and indexFactory @spec @implemented
- indexGrok uses indexOf-based line iteration for events.jsonl and chat_history.jsonl instead of split(newline), matching indexClaude and indexFactory @spec @implemented
- indexCodex uses indexOf/includes guards on the raw line string before JSON.parse to skip lines that do not contain relevant type markers (session_meta, turn_context, response_item, event_msg), avoiding redundant parse overhead @spec @implemented
- label: capContent truncates Event content (user/assistant text 500, tool_result 1000, thinking 2000) and appends a visible ' … [truncated N chars]' marker so truncation is never silent; parseSession(path, source, { full: true }) disables truncation for a verbatim parse, and 'tracequest messages --full' (alias --no-truncate) uses it so exported sequences replay into an API without elided content
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test test/parse/parse-utils.test.js 2>&1 | grep -q '^# fail 0' && grep -q 'capContent' src/parse/parse-claude.js && grep -q 'full: true\|opts.full\|values.full' src/cli/cli-commands.js src/parse/index.js
  tags: [parse, spec, implemented]

## codex
- label: Codex exec/custom tool_result bodies flatten input_text/output_text content blocks into readable text instead of '[object Object]'
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/parse/parse-codex.test.js test/parse/parse-enrich.test.js
  tags: [spec, codex, parse, implemented]
- label: Codex tool failures follow explicit status, nonzero exit, patch failure and timeout envelopes; successful returned text does not imply failure, and negative checks retain nonzero-exit failures for comparability with Claude
  command: node --test test/parse/codex-tool-outcomes.test.js
  tags: [spec, codex, tool-outcomes, implemented]
- label: Codex tool results preserve confirmed failure evidence through display truncation, and format version 11 invalidates metadata built before explicit failure detection
  id: cdxup
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test test/parse/codex-tool-outcomes.test.js test/sessions/codex-cache-upgrade.test.js
  tags: [spec, codex, implemented]

# render
- label: rendered HTML is a self-contained document with all CSS and JS inline — no external dependencies; max-width 960px
  command: grep -q "960" src/render/render-session-rules.js
- the HTML layout has four sections: header with Source badge, metadata grid, statistics bar, Waveform chart, and collapsible Chapters
- label: Chapter outcome classification (in renderHTML) uses: word-boundary regex detection for correction hints in next prompt (/\b(no|wrong|idiot|revert|undo|actually|instead)\b|not what/i sets ch.corrected), plus multi-factor logic on errors + retries + selfCorrections counts (see code ~3563-3584); produces clean/corrected/struggling; NOT the old simple "error if errors>0 or prompt contains 'no' etc".
  id: 4ju
  command: grep -q "corrected" src/render/render-core-shell.js
- label: the Waveform chart is drawn on a canvas that respects device pixel ratio for retina displays
  command: grep -q "devicePixelRatio" src/render/render-core.js
- Waveform decorations: diamonds at top mark user message boundaries; dashed vertical lines mark gaps longer than 30 seconds
- label: session data is HTML-escaped for XSS protection; JSON closing tags use <\\/ escaping to prevent script injection
  command: grep -q "escapeHTML\|&amp;" src/render/render-core.js
- each Chapter shows: prompt text, tool chips with counts, outcome badge (clean/error/corrected), files touched with operation counts, top 8 commands with exit status
- Source badges are color-coded: claude=purple, codex=teal, factory=yellow, opencode=blue, grok=red
- Waveform, activity timeline and cost chart canvas draw functions (drawWaveform, drawTimeline etc) must call ctx.setTransform(1,0,0,1,0,0) or equivalent reset before ctx.scale(DPR, DPR) every time, so that resize listeners and repeated draws never accumulate transform and always render at correct device pixel ratio without distortion @implemented
- Chapter correction detection (the loop setting ch.corrected before outcome classification) must use word-boundary or negated-alnum checks (e.g. /\b(no|wrong|revert|undo|actually|instead)\b/i ) instead of .includes('no') etc, to prevent false-positive 'corrected' outcomes on prompts containing substrings like 'node', 'nothing', 'note', 'know', 'another' etc @implemented
- id: p0e
  label: canvas drawing and analytics client code lives in src/render/render-analytics-compose.js as ANALYTICS_JS; render-assemble.js places the analytics segment in RENDER_BUNDLE_PARTS after the chapter/UI segments and before MAIN_JS, and render.js embeds only the pre-built RENDER_JS bundle
  tags: [render-source-facts, implemented]
- id: ibd
  label: renderHTML embeds RENDER_JS with ANALYTICS_JS already assembled; render.js no longer imports or interpolates ANALYTICS_JS directly
  tags: [render-source-facts, implemented]
- id: omi
  label: chapter-building and chapter filter code lives in src/render/render-chapters.js as CHAPTERS_JS; render-assemble.js places CHAPTERS_HELPERS_JS before CHAPTERS_JS and UI_CHAPTERS_JS through UI_BUNDLE_PARTS, and render.js embeds only the pre-built RENDER_JS bundle
  tags: [render-source-facts, implemented]
- id: 6mb
  label: renderHTML embeds RENDER_JS with chapter helpers and CHAPTERS_JS already assembled; render.js no longer imports or interpolates CHAPTERS_JS directly
  tags: [render-source-facts, implemented]
- id: o8m
  label: UI_ERRORS_JS lives in src/render/render-ui-errors.js, and UI_BUNDLE_PARTS includes ui-errors before chapters-helpers, CHAPTERS_JS, UI_CHAPTERS_JS, and UI_DETAIL_JS
  command: node --input-type=module -e 'import { UI_ERRORS_JS } from "./src/render/render-ui-errors.js"; import { UI_BUNDLE_PARTS } from "./src/render/render-assemble.js"; const ids = UI_BUNDLE_PARTS.map((p) => p.id); const order = ["ui-errors", "chapters-helpers", "chapters", "ui-chapters", "ui-detail"].map((id) => ids.indexOf(id)); if (order.some((i) => i < 0)) process.exit(1); for (let i = 1; i < order.length; i++) if (order[i - 1] >= order[i]) process.exit(1); if (!UI_ERRORS_JS.includes("function renderErrorSummary")) process.exit(1);'
  tags: [render-ui-facts, implemented]
- id: 3lw
  label: chapter UI rendering code is split across UI_CHAPTERS_JS, UI_DETAIL_JS, and UI_ERRORS_JS; render-assemble.js joins those segments through UI_BUNDLE_PARTS and RENDER_BUNDLE_PARTS instead of importing a monolithic src/render-ui.js
  command: test ! -e src/render/render-ui.js && node --input-type=module -e 'import { UI_CHAPTERS_JS } from "./src/render/render-ui-chapters.js"; import { UI_DETAIL_JS } from "./src/render/render-ui-detail.js"; import { UI_ERRORS_JS } from "./src/render/render-ui-errors.js"; import { UI_BUNDLE_PARTS, RENDER_BUNDLE_PARTS } from "./src/render/render-assemble.js"; const uiIds = UI_BUNDLE_PARTS.map((p) => p.id); const renderIds = RENDER_BUNDLE_PARTS.map((p) => p.id); for (const id of ["ui-errors", "ui-chapters", "ui-detail"]) if (!uiIds.includes(id) || !renderIds.includes(id)) process.exit(1); if (!UI_CHAPTERS_JS.includes("function renderFilterBar") || !UI_CHAPTERS_JS.includes("function applyFilters") || !UI_CHAPTERS_JS.includes("function renderChapters") || !UI_DETAIL_JS.includes("function buildChapterDetail") || !UI_DETAIL_JS.includes("function expandAllChapterDetails") || !UI_ERRORS_JS.includes("function renderErrorSummary")) process.exit(1);'
  tags: [render-ui-facts, implemented]
- id: 2u3
  label: renderHTML embeds the pre-built RENDER_JS bundle, while UI rendering code is assembled at module load from UI_BUNDLE_PARTS rather than rebuilt from UI source parts in the browser
  command: node --input-type=module -e 'import { renderHTML } from "./src/render.js"; import { RENDER_JS } from "./src/render/render-assemble.js"; const html = renderHTML({ sessionId: "fact-ui-embed", startTime: "2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z", events: [{ type: "user", text: "ping", timestamp: "2026-01-01T00:00:00.000Z" }] }); if (!html.includes(RENDER_JS.slice(0, 120)) || html.includes("RENDER_BUNDLE_PARTS") || html.includes("joinBundleParts")) process.exit(1);'
  tags: [render-ui-facts, implemented]
- id: x0x
  label: session viewer CSS lives in src/render/render-session-css.js as SESSION_VIEWER_CSS and is re-exported from src/render/render-css.js as CSS; render.js imports CSS from ./render/render-css.js and puts it in the single style block
  tags: [render-source-facts, implemented]
- id: dwi
  label: renderHTML embeds the CSS re-export in its style block; render.js no longer contains the session viewer CSS rules inline
  tags: [render-source-facts, implemented]
- id: 83y
  label: core client-side helpers live in src/render/render-core.js as CORE_JS; render-assemble.js places CORE_JS in RENDER_BUNDLE_PARTS before the UI and analytics segments, and render.js embeds only the pre-built RENDER_JS bundle
  tags: [render-source-facts, implemented]
- id: 21o
  label: renderHTML embeds RENDER_JS with CORE_JS already assembled; render.js no longer imports or interpolates CORE_JS directly
  tags: [render-source-facts, implemented]
- id: o4xv
  label: DOM interaction and keyboard/navigation code is composed in src/render/render-interactions.js as INTERACTIONS_JS; render-assemble.js places it after MAIN_JS and before SHARE_JS in RENDER_BUNDLE_PARTS, and render.js embeds only the pre-built RENDER_JS bundle
  tags: [render-source-facts, implemented]
- id: hib
  label: renderHTML embeds RENDER_JS with INTERACTIONS_JS already assembled; render.js no longer imports or interpolates INTERACTIONS_JS directly
  tags: [render-source-facts, implemented]
- id: nv6
  label: the client-side render() function lives in src/render/render-main.js as MAIN_JS; render-assemble.js places MAIN_JS after analytics and before interactions in RENDER_BUNDLE_PARTS, and render.js embeds only the pre-built RENDER_JS bundle
  tags: [render-source-facts, implemented]
