  label: renderHTML embeds RENDER_JS with MAIN_JS already assembled; render.js no longer imports or interpolates MAIN_JS directly
  tags: [render-source-facts, implemented]
- id: 3jx
  label: render.js imports RENDER_JS from src/render/render-assemble.js and does not import a UI_JS helper from a monolithic render-ui module; UI_JS is a pre-built constant exported by render-assemble.js for assembly and tests
  command: node --input-type=module -e 'import { readFileSync } from "node:fs"; import { UI_JS } from "./src/render/render-assemble.js"; const src = readFileSync("src/render.js", "utf8"); if (!src.includes("import { RENDER_JS } from \"./render/render-assemble.js\"") || src.includes("render-ui.js") || src.includes("UI_JS")) process.exit(1); if (!UI_JS.includes("function renderErrorSummary") || !UI_JS.includes("function renderFilterBar") || !UI_JS.includes("function buildChapterDetail")) process.exit(1);'
  tags: [render-ui-facts, implemented]
- id: 19s
  label: renderHTML assembles the document from static shell strings, the imported CSS re-export, and pre-built RENDER_JS; render-assemble.js, not render.js, joins the client-side script segments
  tags: [render-source-facts, implemented]
- id: thm
  label: buildChapterDetail in src/render/render-ui-detail.js prefixes its unused idx parameter with _idx, and UI_DETAIL_JS exposes buildChapterDetail and expandAllChapterDetails as part of the assembled viewer UI
  command: node --input-type=module -e 'import { UI_DETAIL_JS } from "./src/render/render-ui-detail.js"; if (!UI_DETAIL_JS.includes("function buildChapterDetail(ch, _idx, detail)") || !UI_DETAIL_JS.includes("function expandAllChapterDetails")) process.exit(1);' && TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'UI_DETAIL_JS exposes buildChapterDetail and expandAllChapterDetails in VM|beforeprint listener expands empty chapter details' test/render/render-ui-detail.test.js
  tags: [render-ui-facts, implemented]
- render-chapters buildChapters pre-caches Object.keys(ch.files) into ch._fileKeys before the dependency analysis loop, and the nested dependency loop reads ch._fileKeys and prev._fileKeys instead of calling Object.keys repeatedly, eliminating redundant object-key enumeration overhead @implemented
- render-chapters chapterMatchesFilter uses the pre-cached ch._fileKeys array instead of calling Object.keys(ch.files) during text-search filter evaluation, eliminating redundant object-key enumeration per chapter per filter keystroke @implemented
- render-chapters buildChapters pre-lowercases chapter filter fields (prompt, lastAssistantText, commands, fileKeys, searches, agents, diffs, gitOps, webOps, thinking, mcpOps) into cached _*Lower properties at build time, and chapterMatchesFilter uses these pre-cached lowercased fields instead of calling toLowerCase() on every filter keystroke, eliminating redundant string operations during filter evaluation @implemented
- render-chapters buildChapters builds a _tokenIndex Set per chapter containing all unique 1-char and 2-char lowercase substrings from all filter-scanned text fields, and chapterMatchesFilter checks ch._tokenIndex.has(query) before iterating nested arrays for short search queries (1-2 chars), providing an early-exit that eliminates redundant full-array iteration on chapters that definitely do not match @implemented
- render.js renderHTML caches its full HTML output by sessionHash/sessionId, event count, last event timestamp, and session end/start time in a bounded LRU cache, so repeated views or exports of the same session skip redundant JSON.stringify and template assembly @implemented
- render-chapters buildChapters pre-caches ch._fileKeys = Object.keys(ch.files) immediately after chapter array construction (and correction detection), before the response-quality, efficiency/token-waste, dependency, and pre-lowercase passes; this ensures ch._fileKeys is always defined (an array) and ch._fileKeys.length succeeds in the efficiency fileCount computation (and all later uses) when rendering any session details page @spec @implemented
- label: render source architecture is validated by a focused test that asserts render.js embeds only CSS and pre-built RENDER_JS while render-assemble.js owns the analytics, chapter, UI, core, main, interaction, and share bundle ordering
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/render/render-source-architecture.test.js
  tags: [render-source-facts, implemented]
- label: rendered session Playwright coverage verifies keyboard navigation, native filter activation, and accessible state updates in a real rendered session viewer
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'rendered session keyboard' test/browser/rendered-session-keyboard.playwright.test.js
  tags: [spec, rendered-session, playwright, accessibility, implemented]

## ui
- label: rendered session URL helpers preserve id-based session handles when filters, chapter hashes, permalinks, export, and markdown links rebuild route state
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'preserves id handles' test/render/render-core-shell.test.js
  tags: [spec, rendered-session, route-context, implemented]

# server
- label: the server has index, detail, export, markdown, raw, compare, and API routes; detail/export/markdown/raw accept /route?id=<sessionHash> and preserve /route?path=<session-path> compatibility
  command: grep -q "\/view" src/routes/index.js
- keyboard shortcuts: "/" focuses search, Escape clears and unfocuses
- label: tracequest serve source livereload watches direct .js files under src/; when one changes it bumps modVersion, broadcasts reload SSE, and hotModules reimports the parse.js, render.js, sessions.js, and browser/browser-page.js entry modules through a per-modVersion src snapshot
  id: 8se
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "src .js change broadcasts reload immediately and bumps modVersion|source wires snapshot imports for parse, render, sessions, browser-page|server-state hotModules gates reload on modVersion" test/server/server-live-reload.test.js test/server/server-state-hotmodules.test.js test/server/mod-version.test.js
  tags: [implemented, server-hot-reload]
- the index page has exactly one search mechanism: the filter bar — it handles structured key:value filtering and free-text search; no other search inputs, overlays, or modals should exist @implemented
- isSessionPath and the four routes (/view, /export, /markdown, /compare) reject opencode:// URIs whose ID part does not match /^[0-9a-f-]{8,}$/i ; invalid URIs return 403 'Forbidden: path is not a session file' (or specific) without reaching parseSession or returning 200 rendered page @implemented
- For filesystem paths under allowed prefixes and all opencode:// URIs, isSessionPath (used by /view /export /markdown /compare) returns false for missing files (!existsSync) or malformed opencode IDs; callers thus return 403 'Forbidden: path is not a session file' without ever calling parseSession or rendering a (bad/empty) 200 page -- eliminating previous 500 parse errors and silent bad renders for invalid ?path= values @implemented
- label: the tracequest serve server watches the 5 session data source roots (grokDir, claudeDir, codexDir, factoryDir, openCodeDb parent) using fs.watch + {recursive:true or file} with debounce, and broadcasts data-update SSE events to existing _lrClients when relevant session data changes
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'data-root .jsonl fs events debounce into one data-update SSE|opencode.db watcher debounces data-update SSE' test/server/server-live-reload.test.js
  tags: [serve-refresh, implemented]
- label: the withLiveReload injected EventSource client handles reload messages with location.reload() unless window._stayLoaded is set (live chat pages suppress src-reload so the conversation document stays mounted), and data-update messages by calling window._refreshData() when the page provides it, falling back to location.reload() only when neither _refreshData nor _stayLoaded is set
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'embeds EventSource wiring for reload and data-update|withLiveReload script calls window._refreshData on data-update' test/server/server-html-helpers.test.js test/browser/browser-client-dashboard.test.js
  tags: [serve-refresh, implemented]
- label: on data-update, the served browser UI debounces a call to fetchSessions(function() { render(); }), refreshing the sessions API payload, stats, liveSessions, and rendered table using the current filter/sort/page state
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'assembled client exposes window._refreshData for SSE data-update|fetchSessions refresh path updates live session paths from API payload' test/browser/browser-client-dashboard.test.js
  tags: [serve-refresh, implemented]
- fmtDuration and fmtDurationMd in server.js share a single internal time-formatting core (formatDuration) with option flags for seconds rounding, minute inclusion, and sub-second label; each public wrapper produces exactly the same output as before for all inputs @implemented
- fmtTokens is the single token-formatting helper in server.js; fmtTokensMd is removed and all markdown call sites use fmtTokens, with identical output for positive inputs @implemented
- The tracequest serve server (src/server.js serve fn + / route) accepts an optional project filter from `tracequest serve --filter <expr>` or a ?filter= query, stores it as _initialFilter, and for initial / load calls findSessions(filter || null) then browserPage(filteredSessions, index) so the embedded data and #sessions table start pre-filtered (no longer always sending 7k+ then client-only narrow) @implemented
- browserPage(sessions, index, initialFilter?) in server.js receives the server-prefiltered list (when tracequest serve --filter tracequest or /?filter= is used), renders the filter-input pre-filled with the value, and the client init code starts with that filter applied so table shows only matching rows from the start @implemented
- The served HTML from the / route in server.js continues to contain an identical inline script block with var ALL, all tool/format/filter/render helpers, chip state, pagination, quick filters, and compare bar logic; the only change is that the script content is produced by browserClientScript(data) imported from ./browser-client.js instead of being a literal template string inside browserPage @implemented
- All client-side JavaScript functions inside browserPage (fmtMcp, getToolClr, timeAgo, shortModel, fmtTokens, formatDuration, fmtDuration, estimateCost, computeGrade, renderDashboard, totalPages, pageStart, pageEnd, updatePageUrl, goToPage, renderPagination, escH, parseToken, matchOne, matchesFilters, addChip, removeChip, clearAll, renderChips, getSuggestions, renderSuggestions, closeSuggestions, highlightSuggestion, acceptSuggestion, sortSessions, applyFilters, renderRow, renderPageBatch, buildQfBar, attachQfListeners, qfHasAny, qfMatchSession, applyQfFilters, findSessionByPath, updateCompareBar) live in src/browser-client.js as an exported browserClientScript(data) function; server.js imports browserClientScript from ./browser-client.js and no longer contains their definitions inline @implemented
- comparePage and its esc helper are extracted from server.js into src/compare.js; server.js imports comparePage from ./compare.js and no longer contains the comparePage or esc definitions inline @implemented
- The HTML template generation from browserPage (the <!DOCTYPE html> through </html> string containing all CSS, DOM structure, filter input, dashboard, qf-bar, sort bar, sessions container, pagination, compare bar, and inline script tag) lives in src/browser-page.js as an exported browserPageHTML(data, filterVal) function; server.js imports browserPageHTML from ./browser-page.js and no longer contains the HTML template literal inline @implemented
- server.js no longer imports browserClientScript directly; src/browser-page.js imports browserClientScript from ./browser-client.js and interpolates it into the HTML template it returns; the served HTML from the / route is byte-identical to before the extraction for all inputs @implemented
- isSessionPath, withLiveReload, buildDeltaRowHTML, and projectLabel are defined in src/server-helpers.js and imported by server.js; server.js no longer contains their inline definitions @implemented
- The behavior of all routes in server.js (/view, /export, /markdown, /compare, /) remains identical after extracting isSessionPath, withLiveReload, buildDeltaRowHTML, and projectLabel to src/server-helpers.js; each helper produces the same output for the same inputs as before @implemented
- Server state variables (lrClients, _modVersion, _initialFilter), source file watchers, data root watchers, triggerDataUpdate, and hotModules are defined in src/server-state.js and imported by server.js; server.js no longer contains their inline definitions @implemented
- The behavior of all routes in server.js (/view, /export, /markdown, /compare, /, /__livereload) remains identical after extracting server state to src/server-state.js; each route handler produces the same responses for the same inputs as before @implemented
- server-helpers.js exports a fetchSession(url, parseSession, res, pathParam?, sourceParam?) helper that centralizes path extraction, isSessionPath validation, parseSession invocation with try/catch, and error response sending (400 Missing path, 403 Forbidden, 500 Error parsing session); it returns the parsed session or null when an error response has already been sent @implemented
- server-helpers.js exports a send(res, status, body, contentType?) helper that centralizes response writing: sets optional Content-Type header, calls writeHead(status, headers), and calls res.end(body); all HTTP error responses in server.js routes use send instead of inline res.writeHead + res.end @implemented
- All single-session routes in server.js (/view, /export, /markdown) and both session loads in /compare use fetchSession from server-helpers.js instead of repeating inline path extraction, validation, try/catch, and error response code; the behavior (status codes, error messages, response bodies) remains identical for all valid and invalid inputs @implemented
- The esc(s) HTML-escape helper is defined exactly once in src/server-helpers.js and imported by both src/render.js and src/compare.js; neither render.js nor compare.js contains an inline esc definition @implemented
- The esc helper in server-helpers.js produces identical output to the previous inline definitions in render.js and compare.js: it escapes &, <, >, and " characters using the same replacement sequence @implemented
- Each HTTP route handler (/__livereload, /, /view, /export, /markdown, /compare) is defined as a named exported function in src/routes.js; server.js imports all route handlers from ./routes.js and no longer contains inline route handler bodies @implemented
- server.js is purely server startup and route wiring: it creates the HTTP server, sets up error handling, starts listening, and delegates all request handling to imported route functions from ./routes.js; server.js contains no inline route handler logic beyond dispatching to the imported handler @implemented
- The behavior of all routes (/__livereload, /, /view, /export, /markdown, /compare) remains identical after extracting route handlers to src/routes.js; each route produces the same responses (status codes, headers, body content) for the same inputs as before @implemented
- server.js uses a route map (dictionary/object) to dispatch requests to handler functions instead of sequential if-statements; all 6 routes (/__livereload, /, /view, /export, /markdown, /compare) are registered in the map and the handler lookup produces identical behavior for valid and invalid paths @implemented
- server.js contains a single async handle(req, res) function that dispatches requests via ROUTE_MAP and catches errors with a 500 response; no separate handleAsync wrapper function exists @implemented
- ROUTE_MAP is defined in src/routes.js and exported from there; server.js imports ROUTE_MAP from ./routes.js and no longer defines the route mapping dictionary locally @implemented
- server.js no longer imports individual route handler functions (handleLivereload, handleIndex, handleView, handleExport, handleMarkdown, handleCompare) directly from ./routes.js; it imports only ROUTE_MAP which contains the handler references @implemented
- In src/server-helpers.js send(), the redundant intermediate variable headers is eliminated; the ternary is passed directly to res.writeHead @implemented
- The filter bar accepts boolean expressions with AND, OR, NOT operators and parentheses for arbitrary grouping (e.g. 'project:foo AND (tool:Read OR tool:Edit)', 'NOT source:grok', 'foo AND bar'); bare terms default to AND; individual tokens still support key:value and -prefix negation; the expression is parsed into an AST and evaluated per session; chips are replaced by a single expression input that displays the raw expression text @implemented
- server-helpers withLiveReload computes the live-reload script insertion point in O(1) by using html.endsWith with a known suffix and a constant-offset slice from html.length, instead of scanning the entire HTML string with O(n) lastIndexOf("</body>") @implemented
- server-helpers esc uses a module-scope pre-compiled regex with a lookup-table replacement callback instead of 4 sequential inline .replace() calls, reducing intermediate string allocations from 4 per invocation to 1, with an early-exit test for inputs that contain no escape characters @implemented
- label: tracequest serve source livereload watches direct .js files under src/ plus direct .js helper files inside src/render/, src/server/, and src/browser/; any watched source edit bumps modVersion, broadcasts reload SSE, and hotModules reimports parse.js, render.js, sessions.js, and browser/browser-page.js from a per-modVersion src snapshot so static nested helper imports in those helper directories are refreshed
  id: eak
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "nested src helper .js change broadcasts reload immediately and bumps modVersion|hotModules reimports nested helper modules from a fresh src snapshot after modVersion changes" test/server/server-live-reload.test.js test/server/server-state-hotmodules.test.js
  tags: [server-hot-reload, implemented]
- browser client script must not reset _liveSessions to empty after _INIT_DATA assigns liveSessions from the server embed @spec @implemented
- label: server session routes accept sessionHash query handles while preserving full path and OpenCode URI compatibility
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 test/routes/session-hash-routes.test.js
  tags: [spec, session-hash, implemented]
- label: tracequest serve refreshes served root HTML after a nested browser helper edit in a real subprocess: the source watcher sends reload SSE, modVersion invalidates route output, and the next / response includes the edited helper output
  command: node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'nested browser helper edit refreshes served root HTML after reload' test/bin/tracequest-livereload-integration.test.js
  tags: [spec, server-hot-reload, implemented]

## qf
- clicking source or model quick-filter chips (qf-chips) in the served list view filters the sessions table to matching entries (source exact, model via shortModel); supports toggle/clear; server-side filtering via new model/source query params ensures correct totals, stats, and pagination @implemented
- clicking source or model qf filter badges updates the main filter input field (replacing any prior same-key term while preserving other parts of the expr) so the applied filter is visible/editable in the primary control; deselecting clears the term from the field @implemented

# sessions
- id: q0r
  label: findSessions() scans seven locations: ~/.claude/projects, ~/.codex/sessions, ~/.cursor/projects, the cursor-cloud import root ~/.local/share/tracequest/cursor-cloud (TRACEQUEST_CURSOR_CLOUD_DIR override), ~/.factory/sessions, ~/.grok/sessions, ~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db
  command: grep -qE "claude/projects|codex/sessions|factory/sessions|grok/sessions|opencode" src/sessions/session-discovery.js
