- label: sessions are returned sorted by mtime descending (newest first)
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'findSessions list is mtime-desc|scan failure still returns mtime-desc sorted sessions|findSessions uses mock sidecar scan and coerces mtime-desc' test/sessions.test.js test/sessions/session-index-core.test.js test/sidecar-gate.test.js
  tags: [session-manual-facts, implemented]
- label: peekSession() reads only a 512KiB JSONL prefix for fast metadata extraction; buildIndex() stores metadata in ~/.cache/tracequest/index.json and full-text term frequencies in the separate SearchIndex/search.idx, reusing mtime-matched metadata only when the SearchIndex already contains that session
  id: wkq
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'peekSession misses late prompt beyond 512KiB prefix; full index still indexes it|buildIndex loads matching disk cache entry and skips full re-index when mtime matches|after buildIndex runs with no search.idx, searchSessions finds sessions' test/sessions/peek-session-index-cache.test.js test/sessions/bm25-search.test.js
  tags: [sessions-index-cache-facts]
- label: OpenCode sessions use a virtual path format (opencode://sessionId) and estimate file size as msg_count * 1024
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'queries SQLite and caches rows by DB mtime|includes sessions with exactly 3 messages' test/sessions/session-discovery.test.js
  tags: [session-manual-facts, implemented]
- label: non-existent source directories are silently skipped; malformed session files are caught and skipped
  command: grep -q "existsSync" src/sessions/session-discovery.js
- label: peekOpenCode (invoked by peekSession for source=opencode) reads OpenCode SQLite message parts to derive firstPrompt from user text, model from message.modelID, termFreqs from the title plus indexable text/reasoning parts, and normalized tools from tool parts; it returns no searchText field and falls back to the session title when DB content is unavailable
  id: orb
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'reads prompts, model, and tools from opencode SQLite schema|peekOpenCode falls back to session title when database is unavailable|peekOpenCode indexes reasoning parts into termFreqs like indexOpenCode' test/sessions/session-peek.test.js
  tags: [implemented, opencode-peek-facts]
- label: OpenCode SQLite access in production source uses the shared session-discovery-paths loader helpers, and loadDatabaseSync suppresses node:sqlite ExperimentalWarning while requiring DatabaseSync
  id: v9n
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "OpenCode SQLite production access stays behind the shared warning-suppressing loader" test/sessions/session-discovery-source-contracts.test.js
  tags: [implemented, session-source-contracts]
- label: filesystem session discovery helpers append matches into the caller-provided output array and traverse provider directories with readdirSync({ withFileTypes: true }) to avoid redundant per-entry lstat/stat calls
  id: wsm
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern "filesystem discovery helpers use Dirent traversal and shared output arrays" test/sessions/session-discovery-source-contracts.test.js
  tags: [implemented, session-source-contracts]
- label: sessions buildIndex uses an in-memory cache keyed by the index file's mtime to skip redundant fs.readFileSync and JSON.parse calls when ~/.cache/tracequest/index.json has not changed between invocations
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'buildIndex skips redundant disk read when index file mtime is unchanged|reuses in-memory cache on repeat loadIndexFile' test/sessions.test.js test/index-writers.test.js
  tags: [implemented, session-manual-facts]
- label: sessions findOpenCodeSessions uses an in-memory cache keyed by the SQLite DB file mtime to skip redundant DatabaseSync connection, prepare, and query execution when ~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db has not changed between invocations
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'findOpenCodeSessions skips redundant DB query when SQLite DB mtime is unchanged|queries SQLite and caches rows by DB mtime' test/sessions.test.js test/sessions/session-discovery.test.js
  tags: [implemented, session-manual-facts]
- label: sessions scanSessionForQuery uses a bounded LRU cache of file text content keyed by filePath + fileSize + mtime to skip redundant fs.openSync/fs.readSync/fs.closeSync disk I/O when the same session file is scanned repeatedly across multiple search queries
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'searchSessions skips redundant disk read when mtime unchanged|invalidates scan cache when session file mtime changes|scan cache is bounded and still returns correct results after eviction' test/sessions/scan-queries.test.js
  tags: [implemented, session-manual-facts]
- label: sessions buildIndex reuses a cached Map instance when the disk cache mtime matches and no sessions are stale, eliminating redundant new Map() allocation and result.set() calls on repeated invocations with unchanged data
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'buildIndex returns the identical Map instance on repeated calls with unchanged data|warm buildIndex Map reuse returns same instance without re-indexing|result map cache hit: identical Map when sessions, checksum, and index mtime unchanged' test/sessions.test.js test/sessions/peek-session-index-cache.test.js test/index-writers.test.js
  tags: [implemented, session-manual-facts]
- label: synthetic Claude session generator in test/helpers/synthetic-sessions.js produces JSONL with user prompts assistant replies tool calls and progress filler
  command: test -f test/helpers/synthetic-sessions.js && grep -q makeClaudeSessionLines test/helpers/synthetic-sessions.js && grep -q writeSyntheticClaudeSessions test/helpers/synthetic-sessions.js
  tags: [implemented]
