# cli-refactor
- The CLI uses subcommands instead of flat flags: `tracequest render <file>`, `tracequest messages <file>|--latest`, `tracequest list [project]`, `tracequest latest [project]`, `tracequest find [expr]`, `tracequest search <query>`, `tracequest handoff <query>`, `tracequest standup [project]`, `tracequest share [session]`, `tracequest serve [options]`, and `tracequest presets`; legacy flat flags (--list, --latest, --serve) are removed @implemented
- The CLI parser is built on `node:util.parseArgs` with per-subcommand option definitions, eliminating the 100-line manual argv loop @implemented
- The `serve` subcommand accepts explicit `--port`/`-p` and `--filter`/`-f` options, falls back to preset/default port when omitted, and does not use flat `--serve` mode dispatch @implemented
- The CLI outputs colored, structured messages: errors in red, success in green, metadata in dim; a minimal inline ANSI helper is used to keep zero dependencies @implemented
- The `presets` subcommand lists built-in presets from the presets/ directory with their parsed configuration @implemented
- `--help` text is maintained in `src/cli/cli-help.js` and checked against documented CLI usage examples so the shared help output stays synchronized with the parser surface @implemented
- All existing behavior (render file, list sessions, serve with filter, open browser, preset loading) is preserved under the new subcommand syntax @implemented

# sidecar
- The Rust scan command uses jwalk for parallel directory walking across all provided roots @spec @scan @implemented
- The Rust scan command infers the source type (claude, codex, cursor, factory, grok, opencode) from each root path and applies source-specific directory layout decoding @spec @scan @implemented
- Codex scan recursively finds rollout-*.jsonl files and extracts project from the first line session_meta payload cwd @spec @scan @implemented
- The Rust scan command applies the optional --filter argument to project names and workspace names case-sensitively matching JS behavior @spec @scan @implemented
- OpenCode scan detects the opencode.db path but defers SQLite session extraction to iter 3 @spec @scan @implemented
- The Rust scan command outputs a JSON array of Session objects to stdout with field names matching JS findSessions exactly @spec @scan @implemented
- Claude scan decodes project from the parent directory name and discovers .jsonl files plus subagents subdirectory sessions @spec @scan @implemented
- Grok scan URL-decodes workspace names and walks to chat_history.jsonl depth returning session directory as path @spec @scan @implemented
- Factory scan decodes project from workspace name via regex replace -home-USER-code- and -home-USER- @spec @scan @implemented
- The Rust sidecar includes unit tests for source-specific path parsing and project extraction logic @spec @scan @implemented
- label: The Rust index command reads existing metadata cache at --index-path, validates _v version matches --version, reuses mtime-matched entries only when the session is not search-stale, and re-parses search-stale sessions so stdout can include fresh termFreqs for Node SearchIndex insertion
  id: its
  command: cd sidecar && cargo test test_build_index_reparses_search_stale_cache_hit_for_term_freqs
  tags: [spec, index, implemented, sidecar-cache-reuse-facts]
- The Rust index command implements per-source parsers for claude, codex, cursor, factory, grok, and opencode matching the JS indexer behavior @spec @index @implemented
- The Rust index command normalizes tool names with the same canonical mapping and mcp__ prefix preservation as JS normalizeToolName @spec @index @implemented
- The Rust index command uses memmap2 for session files larger than 512KB and BufReader streaming for smaller files @spec @index @implemented
- label: The Rust index command outputs a JSON object keyed by session path whose IndexEntry values include metadata fields; freshly parsed and search-stale entries also include transient termFreqs for Node SearchIndex insertion, and termFreqs is stripped before index.json persistence and before JS buildIndex returns metadata
  id: gbe
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'buildIndex sends searchStale stdin to sidecar, inserts termFreqs into SearchIndex, and drops searchText|sidecar-emitted termFreqs are stripped from index.json and persisted in search.idx' test/sidecar-gate.test.js test/index-writers.test.js && cd sidecar && cargo test test_build_index_keeps_term_freqs_for_stdout_but_cache_omits_them
  tags: [spec, index, implemented, sidecar-index-output-facts]
- The Rust sidecar includes unit tests for tool normalization, JSONL parsing, and disk cache read logic @spec @index @implemented
- label: Node findSessions delegates to tracequest-sidecar scan --roots <json> [--filter <str>] only when the sidecar gate is open and a valid sidecar path is resolved; successful scan stdout is the complete session list, mtime milliseconds are converted to Date objects, and results are sorted newest first
  id: 507
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'findSessions uses mock sidecar scan and coerces mtime-desc|successful sidecar scan does not merge JS-discovered paths' test/sidecar-gate.test.js test/sessions/session-index-core.test.js
  tags: [node, integration, implemented, sidecar-gate-facts]
- label: Node sidecar detection is disabled only by TRACEQUEST_NO_SIDECAR=1; otherwise TRACEQUEST_SIDECAR_PATH may force an executable, then bundled release/debug ELF binaries are checked, then PATH is queried for tracequest-sidecar, with non-ELF bundled or PATH candidates ignored
  id: sxd
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'only literal 1 activates the gate|gate active skips spawn even when mock binary is installed|sidecar-parity skips when release/debug binary is not a built ELF|resetIndexWritersForTests clears cached sidecar path after env/binary change|SIDECAR_SKIP_ENV documents the only sidecar disable env var' test/sidecar-gate.test.js
  tags: [node, integration, implemented, sidecar-gate-facts]
- label: Node buildIndex delegates stale session indexing to tracequest-sidecar index --index-path <path> --version <int> --sessions-stdin --term-freqs only when the sidecar gate is open; stdin is a JSON object with sessions and searchStale, and stdout entries are merged into the metadata Map after termFreqs is stripped into the SearchIndex
  id: 1j6
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'buildIndex sends searchStale stdin to sidecar, inserts termFreqs into SearchIndex, and drops searchText' test/sidecar-gate.test.js
  tags: [node, integration, implemented, sidecar-gate-facts]
- label: Node sessions.js falls back to the JS findSessions and buildIndex implementations when the sidecar gate is closed, no valid binary is resolved, sidecar stdout cannot be parsed, spawning fails, or the sidecar exits non-zero
  id: 3zy
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'runSidecar returns null for scan when gate is active|findSessions uses JS discovery when TRACEQUEST_NO_SIDECAR=1|buildIndex indexes via JS when TRACEQUEST_NO_SIDECAR=1|runSidecar returns null when no sidecar binary exists|warns and returns null when mock sidecar exits non-zero with stderr|warns when stdout parse fails on zero exit|warns when sidecar binary cannot be executed' test/sidecar-gate.test.js test/sessions/warn-sidecar.test.js
  tags: [node, integration, implemented, sidecar-gate-facts]
- package.json includes a build:sidecar script that runs cargo build --release in the sidecar directory @node @build @implemented
- The Rust scan_opencode function queries ~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db via rusqlite, reads the sessions table, and returns Session structs with path opencode://<id>, project from directory, file as id, size as msg_count*1024, mtime from time_updated, source opencode, and title @opencode @scan @implemented
- Node buildIndex passes the session list to tracequest-sidecar index on stdin via --sessions-stdin so large session lists do not exceed ARG_MAX @spec @node @integration @implemented
- The sidecar index command accepts --sessions-stdin to read the session JSON array from stdin instead of --sessions-json @spec @implemented
- label: Rust build_index indexes 32000 synthetic Claude sessions under 15s
  command: cd sidecar && cargo test test_build_index_synthetic_multi_session_perf -- --nocapture 2>&1 | grep -q 'test result: ok'
  tags: [implemented]

