# docs

## ui
- label: UI style guidelines document the existing tracequest visual language: shared tokens, dense session workflows, panel geometry, status color semantics, typography, responsive behavior, and chart/print conventions
  command: test -f docs/ui-style-design-guidelines.md && grep -q 'Shared Tokens' docs/ui-style-design-guidelines.md && grep -q 'Dense Session Workflows' docs/ui-style-design-guidelines.md && grep -q 'Status Semantics' docs/ui-style-design-guidelines.md && grep -q 'Charts And Print' docs/ui-style-design-guidelines.md
  tags: [spec, docs, ui, implemented]
- label: UI style guidelines document component-specific rules for filters, metrics dashboards, session rows, detail views, modals, buttons and controls, and recurring inspection components
  command: grep -q '## Component Patterns' docs/ui-style-design-guidelines.md && grep -q '### Filters And Query Controls' docs/ui-style-design-guidelines.md && grep -q '### Dashboards And Metrics' docs/ui-style-design-guidelines.md && grep -q '### Session Rows And Lists' docs/ui-style-design-guidelines.md && grep -q '### Chapter And Detail Views' docs/ui-style-design-guidelines.md && grep -q '### Modals And Overlays' docs/ui-style-design-guidelines.md && grep -q '### Buttons And Compact Controls' docs/ui-style-design-guidelines.md
  tags: [spec, docs, ui, component-guidelines, implemented]
- label: UI style guidelines document accessibility, focus states, keyboard shortcuts, print/PDF behavior, and responsive behavior for future UI work
  command: node -e "const fs=require('fs'); const s=fs.readFileSync('docs/ui-style-design-guidelines.md','utf8'); const required=['## Accessibility, Focus, Keyboard, Print, And Responsive Behavior','### Accessibility And Semantics','### Focus And Keyboard Behavior','### Print And PDF Behavior','### Responsive And Touch Behavior','/','j','k','Enter','Escape','@media print','600px','768px','900px']; for (const token of required) { if (!s.includes(token)) { console.error('missing '+token); process.exit(1); } }"
  tags: [spec, docs, ui, accessibility-guidelines, implemented]
- label: UI style guidelines include screenshot-oriented examples grounded in existing browser, compare, and rendered session surfaces, with exact capture targets and visual inspection criteria for each example
  command: grep -q '## Screenshot-Oriented Examples' docs/ui-style-design-guidelines.md && grep -q 'Browser: session list and detail shell' docs/ui-style-design-guidelines.md && grep -q 'Compare: paired session analysis' docs/ui-style-design-guidelines.md && grep -q 'Rendered session: print-ready conversation detail' docs/ui-style-design-guidelines.md
  tags: [spec, docs, ui, visual-examples, implemented]
- label: UI style guidelines document compare-view-specific rules for comparative metric tables, deltas, mirrored tool bars, chapter-quality bars, paired session panels, empty/error states, and visual hierarchy
  command: grep -q '## Compare View Design Patterns' docs/ui-style-design-guidelines.md && grep -q '### Comparative Metric Tables And Deltas' docs/ui-style-design-guidelines.md && grep -q '### Mirrored Tool Bars' docs/ui-style-design-guidelines.md && grep -q '### Chapter-Quality Bars' docs/ui-style-design-guidelines.md && grep -q '### Empty, Error, And Sparse States' docs/ui-style-design-guidelines.md && grep -q '### Visual Hierarchy' docs/ui-style-design-guidelines.md
  tags: [spec, docs, ui, compare-guidelines, implemented]
- label: UI screenshot examples can be refreshed with a maintainer command that writes browser, compare, and rendered-session screenshots to docs/ui-examples/ from current UI builders
  command: test -x scripts/refresh-ui-examples.mjs && node -e "const fs=require('fs'); const pkg=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync('package.json','utf8')); const doc=fs.readFileSync('docs/ui-style-design-guidelines.md','utf8'); if (pkg.scripts['docs:ui-examples'] !== 'node scripts/refresh-ui-examples.mjs') process.exit(1); for (const token of ['npm run docs:ui-examples','scripts/refresh-ui-examples.mjs','docs/ui-examples/browser-index.png','docs/ui-examples/compare-analysis.png','docs/ui-examples/rendered-session-detail.png']) if (!doc.includes(token)) process.exit(1);"
  tags: [spec, docs, ui, visual-examples, screenshot-refresh, implemented]
- label: UI style guidelines define a lightweight visual review convention for refreshed screenshot examples: rerun command, changed screenshot meaning, reviewer inspection points, and intentional versus suspicious diff handling
  command: node -e "const doc=require('fs').readFileSync('docs/ui-style-design-guidelines.md','utf8'); for (const token of ['Visual Review For Refreshed Examples','npm run docs:ui-examples','Changed screenshot files are review prompts','Intentional diffs should be accepted','Suspicious diffs should be investigated']) if (!doc.includes(token)) process.exit(1);"
  tags: [spec, docs, ui, visual-examples, visual-review, implemented]
- label: rendered analytics waveform and cost chart canvases expose keyboard-accessible jump alternatives with focusable canvases, explicit accessible names, and Enter/Space chapter activation matching pointer clicks
  command: node --test test/render/render-analytics-charts.test.js
  tags: [spec, ui, analytics, accessibility, canvas, implemented]
- label: rendered analytics waveform and cost chart keyboard interactions are covered by browser tests for focusability, Arrow/Home/End selection, and Enter/Space chapter jumps
  command: TRACEQUEST_SKIP_LR_WATCH=1 node --test --test-concurrency=1 --test-name-pattern 'rendered analytics chart keyboard' test/browser/rendered-session-keyboard.playwright.test.js
  tags: [spec, ui, analytics, accessibility, canvas, playwright, implemented]
- label: UI style guidelines link to the rendered hover diagnostics audit so future hover-helper work can find the audit decisions and follow-up checklist from the main design guide
  command: grep -q 'rendered-hover-diagnostics-audit.md' docs/ui-style-design-guidelines.md && grep -q 'Rendered hover diagnostics' docs/ui-style-design-guidelines.md
  tags: [spec, docs, ui, hover-diagnostics, discoverability, implemented]
- label: rendered session view route failures render a compact HTML error state with the failed handle, HTTP status, message, and back link instead of a plain-text body
